Title: THE FINISHER — EVIDENCE TEST
Credit: Live research test fixture
Draft date: 20 August 2026

TITLE CARD: THIS IS A TRUE STORY.

TITLE CARD: This test discusses real people and historical events.

FADE IN:

INT. SPORTS NEWSROOM - DAY

A photograph of the 2011 Cricket World Cup final fills a monitor. The names
MS DHONI, GAUTAM GAMBHIR and SRI LANKA are visible on a research board.

ANIKA, a fact checker, reviews a draft with RAVI, a sports writer.

RAVI
India played Sri Lanka in the 2011 ICC Cricket World Cup final in Mumbai on
2 April 2011.

ANIKA
MS Dhoni captained India in that final.

RAVI
Dhoni scored an unbeaten 91 from 79 balls and was named Player of the Match.

ANIKA
India won the final by six wickets, reaching 277 for four with ten balls
remaining.

Ravi points to a paused image of the final delivery.

RAVI
Dhoni sealed the victory by hitting Nuwan Kulasekara for six over long-on.

ANIKA
Gautam Gambhir scored 97 in the same run chase.

RAVI
Before that World Cup victory, Dhoni had already led India to the inaugural
ICC World Twenty20 title in 2007.

ANIKA
And BCCI described Dhoni as hailing from Ranchi, Jharkhand.

Ravi notices a line in the draft and circles it in red.

RAVI
This sentence says, "MS Dhoni scored 97 in the 2011 World Cup final."

ANIKA
That is incorrect. Dhoni scored 91 not out. Gautam Gambhir scored 97.

RAVI
Replace it with: "MS Dhoni scored an unbeaten 91 in the 2011 World Cup
final and finished the chase with a six."

Anika removes an unlicensed ICC CRICKET WORLD CUP logo from the proposed
title card and replaces it with plain text.

ANIKA
The historical facts can be checked against the record. Use of the ICC logo
is a separate trademark and clearance question.

FADE OUT.

THE END
